    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d353">

                <pb facs="0496" n="484" xml:id="pg484"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 P.W./5–2845: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hurley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-28T17:00:00+07:00">May 28, 1945—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 29—2:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>863. Although the Department will, of course, have been fully informed by our
                    Embassy in Lisbon of the recent Japanese peace feeler, I submit as of probable
                    interest the following summary of a telegram from Chang Chien, Chinese Minister
                    there, which has been made available by the Acting Foreign Minister:<anchor
                        n="10" xml:id="d353-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>[Here follows summary of telegram similar to telegram 990, May 7, noon, from
                    Lisbon, printed on <ref target="#pg478">page 478</ref>.]</p>
                <p>When handing this message to Briggs,<anchor n="11" xml:id="d353-f2"/> Wu stated
                    that the Chinese Foreign Office had already replied, declaring that China will
                    accept nothing less than unconditional surrender of Japan. He also commented
                    upon the “obvious effort” of Japan to sow suspicion of Russia.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hurley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
